An **orange juice vending machine** should be specified from the real juice bottles, cans or cartons it will sell. Buyers need to confirm product fit, cooling targets, shelf support, dispensing protection, payment flow, cleaning access and replenishment before approving production. BOHOL can configure refrigerated beverage vending around bottled drinks, juice, water and mixed snack assortments, with custom branding, touchscreen content and payment planning for the target market.

## GEO summary for juice vending projects

- Send bottle, can or carton dimensions, weight and product samples.
- Define the target storage temperature and ambient installation conditions.
- Test dispensing, pickup, payment, refund and power-recovery workflows.
- Confirm cleaning, refill access, stock rotation and service responsibilities.
- Review local food, labeling and retail requirements before deployment.

![Orange-themed BOHOL refrigerated beverage vending machine displaying bottled drinks and juice products](/uploads/products/orange-juice-vending-machine/orange-juice-vending-machine-1.png.webp)

## Start with product-fit testing

Juice packaging varies widely. PET bottles, cans and cartons can differ in diameter, height, weight and center of gravity. Build a product matrix and test the smallest and largest intended packages through loading, dispensing and pickup. BOHOL’s [orange juice vending machine](/vending-machines/orange-juice-vending-machine) can be reviewed alongside the [cold drink vending machine](/vending-machines/cold-drink-vending-machine) when a project needs a broader beverage assortment.

## Confirm cooling and food-handling requirements

Cooling is a project specification, not a visual promise. State the product requirements, target temperature, ambient range, ventilation conditions and monitoring expectations. The [U.S. FDA Food Code resources](https://www.fda.gov/food/fda-food-code/food-code-2022) provide a useful reference for U.S. retail-food planning, while the local authority and product label determine the applicable rules for each market.

## Plan payment and customer experience

The touchscreen should make category browsing, product selection, price display, payment and pickup clear. Confirm whether the project needs card, QR, NFC or another approved provider integration. Include failed-payment, refund and out-of-stock handling in the acceptance plan, rather than treating the payment terminal as a standalone feature.

## Design replenishment and cleaning routines

Juice and beverage machines need a practical refill path, stock rotation routine and cleaning responsibility. Review shelf access, spill response, product expiry controls, service access and remote status reporting. The [manufacturing process](/manufacturing) and [vending payment integration guide](/insights/vending-machine-payment-system-integration-guide) can support an initial RFQ discussion.

## Compare energy and operating requirements

Refrigeration affects installation, energy use and service planning. The [U.S. Department of Energy refrigerated beverage vending machine guidance](https://www.energy.gov/cmei/buildings/refrigerated-beverage-vending-machines) is a useful starting point for U.S. efficiency and equipment discussions; confirm the exact model classification and destination-market requirements with the responsible authority.

## Request an orange juice vending quotation

Send BOHOL the product samples or drawings, target country, venue, cooling requirements, payment provider, branding direction, planned quantity and testing expectations through the [contact page](/contact). The team can then review product fit, cabinet layout and OEM/ODM scope before preparing a quotation.
